  "slug": "association-adjusting-2e22",
  "summary": "New tools and resources tie fine-mapped GWAS signals to cell types, RNA features and enhancer-gene links, with type 2 diabetes as a recurring test case.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is moving from GWAS loci to effector genes and the cellular contexts in which they act. CELL-X carries fine-mapped T2D genes into islet single-cell atlases for beta-cell prioritization, and a multi-layer colocalization study of 338 T2D signals extends beyond gene expression to GTEx adipose exon, transcript and splice-junction usage. EPIC2 links GWAS summary statistics to single-cell chromatin accessibility while accounting for LD to rank trait-relevant cell types. CREMAP removes shared latent variation before testing peak-gene links, aiming to improve enhancer-gene mapping. Resources include CellColocDB, using coloc.abf across bulk, sorted-cell and single-cell data, and the IGVF Catalog knowledge graph with APIs and an LLM interface. SIQReg addresses upstream phenotype scale in biobank analyses.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
